{"name":"Bruised Burgundy","hex":"#5b4148","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bruised","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bruise"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Synonym of debruised."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruised"},{"term":"burgundy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Burgundy (red wine).","A dark red colour tinged with purple, like that of Burgundy (red) wine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep purple red color like that of Burgundy wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burgundy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bruise","blocks":[{"text":"A bruise, also known as a contusion, is a type of hematoma of tissue, the most common cause being capillaries damaged by trauma, causing localized bleeding that extravasates into the surrounding interstitial tissues. Most bruises occur close enough to the epidermis such that the bleeding causes a visible discoloration. The bruise then remains visible until the blood is either absorbed by tissues or cleared by immune system action. Bruises which do not blanch under pressure can involve capillaries at the level of skin, subcutaneous tissue, muscle, or bone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Pferdekuss.jpg/330px-Pferdekuss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruise"},{"title":"Burgundy","blocks":[{"text":"Burgundy is a historical region in France, broadly corresponding to the territory of the former administrative region of the same name, which existed from 1982 to 2015 before it was merged on 1 January 2016 into Bourgogne-Franche-Comté. Its capital is Dijon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Flag_of_Bourgogne.svg/330px-Flag_of_Bourgogne.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgundy"},{"title":"Burgundy (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Burgundy is a purplish, dark-red color. The name comes from the Burgundy wine in France. The word \"burgundy\" is not usually capitalized."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Danish_Passport_Cover.svg/330px-Danish_Passport_Cover.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burgundy_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg/500px-Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg/500px-Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman's bruising after a severe fall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/500px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/1280px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/500px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bruise caused by colliding with a handrail, typical of extreme sports such as skateboarding and rollerblading.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeverebruise.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/500px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/1280px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=e